course: dictionary
lesson: 3902
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «The foxes became friendly and wagged their tails.» Here friendly means gentle and not likely to attack, because the foxes were tame animals.
explain: The same word can also describe how a person behaves. «School audiences are friendly» means they are kind and pleasant, so a performer does not need to feel nervous. When you meet a word with several meanings, ask yourself: which meaning fits this sentence best?
explain: Friendly also appears in other words, like eco-friendly and user-friendly. Look at the word before or after it, and at the whole sentence, to find the meaning.
fact: «Friendly» is an adjective, so it can change to friendlier and friendliest.
fact: «Friendly» means kind and pleasant to others, behaving like a friend.
fact: «Friendly» can describe an animal that is gentle and not likely to attack, but a friendly-seeming dog may still bite, so ask the owner before stroking it.
fact: Words like eco-friendly, child-friendly and user-friendly mean not harmful to, suitable for, or easy for.
fact: In the UK, a friendly is a sport match that is not part of a competition.
exercise: «The foxes became friendly and wagged their tails.» In this sentence, friendly means | *Gentle and not likely to attack | Not harmful to the environment | Kind and pleasant to people | A match that is not part of a competition
exercise: Some football teams play a friendly before the season starts. What is a friendly here? | A kind word to a referee | *A match that is not part of a competition | A tame animal | A safe place to play
exercise: Which word means easy for people to use? | Eco-friendly | Friendly-faced | Child-friendly | *User-friendly
test: Ella says the dog looks friendly, so she can stroke it. What should she do first? | Give it a biscuit | Shout hello at it | *Ask the owner before stroking it | Stroke it quickly before it moves
test: In «a friendly face», what does friendly mean? | A sport game | Not harmful to nature | *Kind and pleasant | Easy to use
exam: Which sentence uses friendly to mean not harmful to nature? | *Mum buys eco-friendly cleaning products | Ahmed made a friendly remark to his teacher | We play a friendly match on Saturday | The stranger gave a friendly smile
